The Problem I Faced

I used to frequently forget to update the build number in pubspec.yaml before creating an Android build.
For example, after creating.
version: 1.0.0+15
I would need to manually remember to change it to:
version: 1.0.0+16
When you're creating multiple builds for QA or testing, this is a small step, but it's easy to miss.

So instead of adding another step to my build checklist, 
I added a pre-build script in the Android/Gradle build process that automatically increments the build number before starting the build.

I have added one dart file which calls auto increment script. this file runs before build creation.
main() {
  _incrementBuildNumber()
}

void _incrementBuildNumber() {
  final file = File('pubspec.yaml');

  if (!file.existsSync()) {
    throw Exception('pubspec.yaml not found');
  }

  final content = file.readAsStringSync();

  final regex = RegExp(
    r'^version:\s*\d+\.\d+\.\d+\+(\d+)\s*$',
    multiLine: true,
  );

  final match = regex.firstMatch(content);

  if (match == null) {
    throw Exception('Version with build number not found in pubspec.yaml');
  }

  final currentBuildNumber = int.parse(match.group(1)!);
  final newBuildNumber = currentBuildNumber + 1;

  final updatedContent = content.replaceFirst(
    match.group(0)!,
    match.group(0)!.replaceFirst(
      '+$currentBuildNumber',
      '+$newBuildNumber',
    ),
  );

  file.writeAsStringSync(updatedContent);

  print('Build number: $currentBuildNumber → $newBuildNumber');
}

===============================================================================
Android side app level build.gradle file add a task 

// Automatically upgrade Flutter build number before any release build
task upgradeBuildNumber {
    doLast {
        def dartExec = org.gradle.internal.os.OperatingSystem.current().isWindows()
                ? "${localProperties.getProperty('flutter.sdk')}/bin/dart.bat"
                : "${localProperties.getProperty('flutter.sdk')}/bin/dart"

        exec {
            workingDir "${rootProject.projectDir}/.."
            commandLine dartExec, 'upgrade_build_number.dart'
        }
    }
}

tasks.configureEach { task ->
    if (task.name.contains('Release') && task.name.startsWith('assemble')) {
        task.dependsOn upgradeBuildNumber
    }
}

This will also be useful in CI/CD pipelines.
